face-image: img/events/brixton_1981.jpg

= The Riots Return

There has been rioting again: in Handsworth in Birmingham, in Brixton, and on the Broadwater Farm estate in Tottenham, where a policeman has been killed. The inner cities are angrier than they were in 1981.

- @riot_police: Back the police, and promise more of them.
- @inner_cities: Put money into the inner cities.

@riot_police
subtitle: The right approves.
on-arrival: right_dissent -= 3; wet_dissent += 3; c1_con += 0.5*(1-dissent); de_lab += 1

The Home Secretary promises more police, better equipment and a review of public order law. The estates are quieter, for now.

@inner_cities
subtitle: -1 budget. The wets approve.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; wet_dissent -= 3; dry_dissent += 2; de_con += 0.5*(1-dissent); ru_london -= 0.2; ru_westmids -= 0.2

Task forces go into the worst estates with money for jobs, training and youth projects. The money is real; whether it is enough is another question.

@anglo_irish
title: Hillsborough
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and second_term = 1 and anglo_irish_seen = 0 and time >= 95
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: anglo_irish_seen = 1
face-image: img/events/westminster.jpg

= Hillsborough

After a year of secret talks, Garret FitzGerald and the Irish government are ready to sign an agreement at Hillsborough Castle. Dublin would get a say in how Northern Ireland is run, through a joint conference with British ministers; in return it would recognise that Northern Ireland stays British as long as a majority wants it to.

- @sign_agreement: Sign the Anglo-Irish Agreement.
- @refuse_agreement: Refuse to give Dublin a role.

@sign_agreement
subtitle: Washington and Dublin are delighted. The Unionists feel betrayed.
on-arrival: anglo_irish = 1; uup_relation -= 25; right_dissent += 6; us_relation += 5; europe_relation += 3; partner_dissent += 4 if govt_type = 2

The Agreement is signed, and Ulster says no. Within weeks every Unionist MP has resigned his seat in protest, and a hundred thousand people rally outside Belfast City Hall. Ian Gow, your friend and former aide, resigns as a Treasury minister.

@refuse_agreement
subtitle: The Unionists are relieved. Washington is not.
on-arrival: uup_relation += 5; us_relation -= 5; right_dissent -= 2; wet_dissent += 2

The talks are shelved. Dublin is bitter, the State Department is disappointed, and the Unionists cannot quite believe their luck.

#################### 1986

@westland
title: Westland
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and second_term = 1 and westland_seen = 0 and time >= 96 and (defence_secretary == "Heseltine" or environment_secretary == "Heseltine")
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: westland_seen = 1
face-image: img/events/cabinet.jpg

= Westland

Westland, Britain's last helicopter maker, is going bust. Its board wants to be rescued by Sikorsky of America; Michael Heseltine is campaigning, inside and outside the Cabinet, for a European consortium instead. He has ignored collective responsibility for weeks, and now a letter from the Solicitor-General that undermines him has been leaked to the press from Leon Brittan's department.

- @back_board: Back the Westland board, and bring Heseltine into line.
- @back_heseltine: Let Heseltine have his European rescue.

@back_board
subtitle: Heseltine walks out. Brittan may have to go too.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heseltine_out = 1;
Q.thatcher_rating -= 6;
Q.rebellion += 2;
Q.wet_dissent += 6;
Q.dry_dissent -= 2;
// Heseltine's department goes to someone else
if (Q.defence_secretary == 'Heseltine') {
    Q.defence_secretary = 'Younger';
    Q.defence_dry = 0;
}
if (Q.environment_secretary == 'Heseltine') {
    Q.environment_secretary = 'Baker';
    Q.environment_dry = 0;
}
// the leak is traced to Brittan's department
if (Q.home_secretary == 'Brittan') {
    Q.home_secretary = 'Hurd';
    Q.home_dry = 0;
}
!}
call: cabinet_recalc

At Cabinet, Heseltine gathers his papers, says he can no longer serve, and walks out into Downing Street to announce his resignation to the cameras. Within a fortnight Leon Brittan has resigned too, over the leaked letter. You tell a friend that you may not be Prime Minister by six o'clock, but you survive the debate, and Heseltine is free to plot on the backbenches.

@back_heseltine
subtitle: Heseltine stays. The dries and the Americans are not pleased.
on-arrival: dry_dissent += 5; us_relation -= 3; thatcher_rating -= 1; wet_dissent -= 2

The government leans on Westland's board to take the European offer. Heseltine is triumphant, the Americans are cross, and the dries ask who is running the government.

@libya
title: The Libyan Raid
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and second_term = 1 and libya_seen = 0 and time >= 100
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: libya_seen = 1
face-image: img/cards/reagan_thatcher.jpg

= The Libyan Raid

After a bomb in a Berlin nightclub killed American servicemen, President Reagan wants to strike back at Colonel Gaddafi, using F-111 bombers based in Britain. He needs your permission tonight.

- @allow_raid: Let the Americans use the British bases.
- @refuse_raid: Refuse.

@allow_raid
subtitle: Washington will not forget it. Most voters disapprove.
on-arrival: us_relation += 8; thatcher_rating -= 3; wet_dissent += 2; europe_relation -= 2

The bombers take off from Lakenheath and Upper Heyford. Two-thirds of the public tell the pollsters they disapprove, but in Washington you have a debt that will be repaid.

@refuse_raid
subtitle: The public approves. Washington is angry.
on-arrival: us_relation -= 8; thatcher_rating += 1; right_dissent += 3

The raid goes ahead from the carriers in the Mediterranean, without British help. The White House lets it be known that it noticed.

@wapping
title: Wapping
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and second_term = 1 and wapping_seen = 0 and time >= 97
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: wapping_seen = 1
face-image: img/events/steel_strike.jpg

= Wapping

Rupert Murdoch has moved The Times, The Sun and the News of the World overnight to a new plant at Wapping, behind razor wire, with electricians in place of the print unions. Five thousand printers have been sacked, and every Saturday night there are pickets and police at the gates.

- @law_course: Let the law take its course.
- @urge_settlement: Urge a settlement.

@law_course
subtitle: The print unions are beaten. The papers are grateful.
on-arrival: union_power -= 3; c1_con += 0.5*(1-dissent); tuc_mood += 3; wet_dissent += 1

The courts restrain the pickets, and the papers come out every night. Within a year the print unions give up, and Fleet Street moves to new plants with new technology.

@urge_settlement
subtitle: The unions are grateful. The papers are not.
on-arrival: tuc_mood -= 3; dry_dissent += 2

The Employment Secretary calls for a settlement. Nobody at Wapping listens.

@teachers
title: The Teachers' Dispute
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and second_term = 1 and teachers_seen = 0 and time >= 90
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: teachers_seen = 1
face-image: img/cards/school.jpg

= The Teachers' Dispute

The teachers' unions have been refusing to cover lessons and run after-school activities for months over pay. Parents are angry with both sides.

- @hold_teachers: Hold the line on pay.
- @settle_teachers: Settle, with new contracts.

@hold_teachers
subtitle: +0.5 budget. The dispute drags on.
on-arrival: budget += 0.5; c1_con -= 1; wet_dissent += 2; dry_dissent -= 1

The dispute rumbles on into another school year. Parents blame the unions first, and the government second.

@settle_teachers
subtitle: -1 budget. Peace in the classroom.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; c1_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 2; dry_dissent += 2

The teachers get a pay rise and new contracts that set out their duties for the first time. The schools are back to normal by the spring.

#################### 1987

@labour_1987
title: Labour's Campaign
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and second_term = 1 and in_campaign = 1 and lab_leader == "Kinnock" and labour_1987_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
